stem="A 58-year-old woman comes to the office for cardiovascular risk assessment. Menarche was at age 13. She had two uncomplicated term pregnancies and breastfed both children. Natural menopause occurred at age 42. She stopped smoking 25 years ago after 3 years of light smoking. Her father had a myocardial infarction at age 76. Her blood pressure is 124/78 mm Hg, and fasting LDL-cholesterol concentration is 118 mg/dL.{FIG}Which of the following factors in her history most increases her cardiovascular risk?",
